## Cross-cutting facts verified (used by several stories)

- X1. First message needs no demand. `TI/ProducerControllerImpl.scala:56-66` (design note), `createState` sets `requestedSeqNr = loadedState.currentSeqNr` (:254), `becomeActive` sends `RequestNext` at start (:331-335). Spec `TT/ProducerControllerSpec.scala:47-72` observes `SequencedMessage(1)` at the consumer probe before any `Request` is sent.
- X2. The producer controller DOES push a resend without being asked: `ResendFirst` timer started whenever `currentSeqNr == firstSeqNr` (`TI/ProducerControllerImpl.scala:422-423`, not conditional on a durable queue), handler :675-685, cancelled on ack of `firstSeqNr` (:548-549), restarted on `RegisterConsumer` with unconfirmed (:706-709). `reference.conf:91-93`: "retries sending the first message with this interval until it has been confirmed". This contradicts the Scaladoc `T/ProducerController.scala:62-64` ("will not push resends unless requested") and the reconciliation texts of #810, #998 and #1165 that tie `ResendFirst` to the durable queue. Spec: `TT/ProducerControllerSpec.scala:47-72` (non-durable; second identical `SequencedMessage(1)` arrives, then `expectNoMessage(1100.millis)` after `Request(1,10,..)`) and :149-185.
- X3. Producer-side resend also triggered by `Request`: `(viaTimeout || newConfirmedSeqNr == s.firstSeqNr) && supportResend` resends all unconfirmed (`TI/ProducerControllerImpl.scala:482-485`). Spec :111-147 (viaTimeout) and :177-179 (`Request(2L,..)` with firstSeqNr 2 resends 3). So a repeated `Request` is idempotent for the window (`requestedSeqNr` only grows, :500) but not free of side effects.
- X4. Sequence scope = (ProducerController ref, seqNr). `producerId` is only a log/MDC label (`T/ProducerController.scala:89-91`) and is overwritten from the latest accepted message (`TI/ConsumerControllerImpl.scala:386`); producer change is detected by `seqMsg.producerController != producerController || receivedSeqNr == 0` (:108-109). `Request`/`Ack`/`Resend` carry no consumer identity (`TI/ProducerControllerImpl.scala:102-114`).
- X5. No delivery spec uses injected time. grep `ManualTime|ManualClock` in `TT/`: none. Timing is real (test config overrides `resend-interval-min` to 1s, `reference.conf` default is 2s with max 30s; `expectNoMessage(1.1.second)`: `TT/ConsumerControllerSpec.scala:30-34,213`).
- X6. D13 for all delivery stories: a Pekko oracle exists (the specs above exercise controller behavior through public commands plus the internal messages `Request/Resend/Ack`). Whether it is applicable as a Go differential scenario is pending determination; missing evidence: how a differential scenario drives the JVM side with internal protocol messages, and which harness hosts `pekko-actor-typed` (judge scope for typed is not established in develop). Never `pending approval` by default.

